[%# I know I'm kind of stealing the term "teenager" here.  -%]
[%# Frankly, I would prefer to just say "hackers", but not -%]
[%# everyone would associate a hacker with someone they'd  -%]
[%# want to talk to - which I find somewhat appropriate.   -%]
[%# Both are, in a way, outcasts of the society, who chal- -%]
[%# lenge its rules so much they are seen as deviants.     -%]
[%#                                                        -%]
[%# But is being an outcast what defines me as a teenager, -%]
[%# as a hacker?  If I were to become one of the accepted  -%]
[%# ones, celebrated by schools for my mischief, sponsored -%]
[%# by the government for my hacks... it to me changes a   -%]
[%# core part of my being -- that is the desire for auto-  -%]
[%# nomy, and supposedly the respect for the autonomy of   -%]
[%# one another, which neither do the authorities hold the -%]
[%# empathy nor care for.  In an idealized outlook for a   -%]
[%# world run by the outcasts we would base our power not  -%]
[%# on the suppression of those deemed inferior by some    -%]
[%# unspeakable criteria inferior, but on the equal power  -%]
[%# we hold under this culture of exchanging knowledge and -%]
[%# sharing information (sharing truly *is* caring, ha! :) -%]
